True, invisibility has that advantage in situations with large open spaces
and crowds. However, once you are in a fight, or in a tight spot where you
can't run around an enemy, invisibility makes the monsters look for you in
a one square radius around your actual position (i.e., they're attacking
those spots until they find the right one). That's a similar effect to that
of displacement, only with displacement you get a two square radius, which
means you get much more fighting time before you have to shift position.

When I have a CoD, I avoid permanent invisibility in order to get this
effect. I can still aquire temporary invisibility when I tackle the
bigroom, the valley or similar. Note that the long range effect of
invisibility is void when you make noise, though.

